  triage:title "Function-length RULE-002 hard violation in drain()" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-daemon/src/peer_drain_coordinator.rs:190-281 contains a drain() function that is 92 lines long, exceeding the enforced 80-line RULE-002 limit. This is a NEW violation introduced in this sprint, directly observable via `just lint` execution failure. The violation is confirmed by execution of the function-length lint check at .just/logs/20260725164730-function-length.log. This is an objective CI-equivalent gate failure, not a judgment call. Fix required: refactor drain() to extract per-page delivery/response-handling logic into a separate function to bring the function under the 80-line limit." ;
